8,(PDF) Musical aspects of Austronesian culture,https://www.academia.edu/4175401/Musical_aspects_of_Austronesian_culture,"August 5, 2013 - Why are bamboo slit-gongs considered a linked cultural element in Austronesian cultures?add · Bamboo slit-gongs, found from Taiwan to New Caledonia and Madagascar, demonstrate a cohesive musical tradition likely disseminated by Austronesian migrations, as seen in Kunst's documented distribution across the Pacific islands.",Pendau,Austronesian
9,Austronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and Southeast Asia | IIAS,https://www.iias.asia/books/austronesian-soundscapes-performing-arts-oceania-and-southeast-asia,"Ramon P. Santos, Ph.D. UP Center for Ethnomusicology ""The island world of the Pacific and Indian oceans, inhabited by peoples speaking Austronesian languages, has an extremely variegated cultural spectrum. This volume is organised as a musical view on the historical map of the Austronesian expansion, attempting for the first time to see how the performing arts contribute to understanding the interlinkages of this immense cultural area and thus providing a fresh and welcome view on these understudied, yet extremely diverse musical cultures.""",Pendau,Austronesian
